I understand that you want to create a Sankey chart that shows the flow of money from ABC suppliers to XYZ, and then to DEF suppliers, with the twist that some of the money is being "cut" or reduced, and you want to visualize this reduction as a link in the Sankey chart.

To achieve this, you can use a combination of D3.js and Sankey.js libraries. Here's a high-level overview of how you can create this chart:

1. First, you need to prepare your data. You'll need to have a dataset that contains the following information:
	* Source node (ABC suppliers)
	* Target node (DEF suppliers)
	* Value (the amount of money being transferred)
	* Reduction value (the amount of money being "cut" or reduced)
2. Next, you'll need to create a Sankey chart using Sankey.js. You can do this by creating a SVG element and adding the necessary attributes and styles.
3. To visualize the reduction, you'll need to create a link between the source and target nodes. You can do this by adding a path element to the SVG and styling it to represent the reduction.
4. To make the link thicker at the head and tail, you can use the `stroke-width` attribute and set it to a larger value for the head and tail nodes, and a smaller value for the link.
5. Finally, you'll need to add some interactivity to the chart, such as hover effects and tooltips, to make it more engaging and informative.

Here's some sample code to get you started:
```html
<div id="sankey-chart"></div>

<script>
  // Load data the
  var data = [
    { source: "ABC1", target: "DEF1", value: 100, reduction: 20 },
    { source: "ABC2", target: "DEF2", value: 200, reduction: 30 },
    { source: "ABC3", target: "DEF3", value: 300, reduction: 40 }
 ];

   // Create the Sankey chart
  var sankey = d3.sankey()
    .nodeWidth(20)
    .nodePadding(10)
    .size([width, height])
    .nodes(data.map(function(d) { return { id: d.source, name: d.source }; }))
    .links(data.map(function(d) { return { source: d.source, target: d.target, value: d.value, reduction: d.reduction }; }));

  // Create the SVG
  var svg = d3.select("#sankey-chart")
    .append("svg")
    .attr("width", width)
    .attr("height", height);

  // Add the nodes
  svg.selectAll("g.node")
    .data(sankey.nodes())
    .enter()
    .append("g")
    .attr("class", "node   ")
 .append("rect")
    .attr("x", function(d) { return d.x; })
    .attr("y", function(d) { return d.y; })
    .attr("width", sankey.nodeWidth())
    .attr("height", sankey.nodeHeight())
    .append("text")
    .attr("x", function(d) { return d.x + 5; })
    .attr("y", function(d) { return d.y + 15; })
    .text(function(d) { return d.name; });

  // Add the links
  svg.selectAll("path.link")
    .data(sankey.links())
    .enter()
    .append("path")
    .attr("class", "link")
    .attr("d", function(d) {
      var source = sankey.nodes().filter(function(n) { return n.id === d.source; })[0];
      var target = sankey.nodes().filter(function(n) { return n.id === d.target; })[0];
      return "M " + source.x + " " + source.y + " L " + target.x + " " + target.y;
    })
    .style("stroke", function(d) { return d.reduction > 0 ? "red" : "black"; })
    .style("stroke-width", function(d) {
      if (d.source === "ABC1" || d.target === "DEF1") {
        return 5;
      } else {
        return 2;
      }
    });

  // Add some interactivity
  svg.selectAll("path.link")
    .on("mouseover", function(d) {
      d3.select(this).style("stroke", "red");
    })
    .on("mouseout", function(d) {
      d3.select(this).style("stroke", function(d) { return d.reduction > 0 ? "red" : "black"; });
    });
</script>
```
